1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,740
In the heart of Seoul stands a kind king. He gave us the letters we use every day — Hangeul. Shall we travel far, far back in time to meet him?

2
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:31,810
Long ago, a prince loved books more than anything. His name was Chungnyeong — one day he’d become the great King Sejong! While his brothers played outside, he slipped into his room to read.

3
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:45,550
His father brought wonderful teachers. His brothers loved archery and riding, but Chungnyeong loved learning best — listening with bright, shining eyes!

4
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:58,780
But he read SO much his eyes turned red! His worried father said, “Time to rest!” and tucked the books away. With no books, Chungnyeong felt so sad.

5
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:11,180
Then one day — ta-da! He found ONE book left behind a screen. “Yes! Found it!” Overjoyed, he read it over and over.

6
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:26,730
He had a lovely reason to learn. More than being clever, he wanted to help people. “If I learn a lot, I can make everyone happier!” That little wish became a great gift.

7
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:39,960
Even grown up, Chungnyeong was still a bookworm! He borrowed every book in the palace — and reread each one a hundred times. “Every time, I find something new!”

8
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:56,160
But it wasn’t only books. Music, the stars at night, healing herbs, numbers — whatever sparked his curiosity, he dove right in. “Everything in the world is amazing!” What a curious young man!

9
00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:10,410
As the third son, it seemed he’d never be king. His eldest brother loved freedom; Chungnyeong loved quietly learning. Different paths — and he happily lost himself in his studies.

10
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:26,290
Chungnyeong was special. Never boastful, kind to everyone — gentle to old ministers and palace workers alike. “That prince is so good-hearted,” people whispered, and the praise spread quietly through the palace.

11
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:46,070
His father, King Taejong, watched Chungnyeong closely. To hard questions, the boy gave wise, clear answers. “With this child’s wisdom, the people would be well cared for.” A big idea began to grow in his father’s heart.

12
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:56,890
In time, Chungnyeong married a kind-hearted bride, Queen Soheon. The two lived happily, caring for each other.

13
00:02:56,890 --> 00:03:12,030
Soon the house was full of children’s laughter. Chungnyeong loved his family as much as his books. And he always wondered the same thing: “How can I make the people happier?”

14
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:23,410
Under a sky full of stars, Chungnyeong looked up quietly. Everyone knew he was the third son — but destiny had a surprise in store.

15
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:36,920
Then, surprise! At twenty-two, Chungnyeong became king. The third son, a king! The whole country was amazed.

16
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:54,190
On the throne, the young king’s hands trembled a little — the job felt so heavy. But Sejong took a deep breath and resolved: “I’m scared, but I’ll do my very best for the people!” And bravely, he took his first step.

17
00:03:54,190 --> 00:04:11,930
Sejong needed clever friends. So he built a wonderful study hall called Jiphyeonjeon and gathered talented young scholars. Reading and debating together — how exciting!

18
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:28,090
The young Sejong was so hard-working! Every single day he held “gyeongyeon,” studying with his scholars, and read reports deep into the night. A king who gave up sleep to study! Even his ministers were amazed.

19
00:04:28,090 --> 00:04:46,100
Sejong didn’t stay only in the palace. He looked closely at how the people lived. When rain didn’t come, he worried about the crops; when it was cold, he worried they were warm. “The people’s daily life IS the country’s strength.”

20
00:04:46,100 --> 00:05:03,140
Many wise ministers stood beside Sejong. With clever helpers like Hwang Hui and Maeng Saseong, he put good ideas into action, one by one. Together, nothing seemed impossible — and the country flourished.

21
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:18,740
But Sejong saw something sad. The people couldn’t read, so when treated unfairly, they couldn’t even write it down. Those hard Chinese characters were just too difficult to learn.

22
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:30,070
Wanting to share good lessons, Sejong made a picture book of kind people’s stories — so even those who couldn’t read could look at the pictures.

23
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:44,140
But pictures weren’t enough. Without reading the words beside them, the deeper meaning was lost. Sejong thought, “What if there were letters anyone could read and write easily?”

24
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:59,840
King Sejong’s heart often ached. Because the people couldn’t read, they couldn’t speak up even when wronged. “It’s the letters,” he thought. “The letters are just too hard.”

25
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:17,480
Even picture books didn’t help if you couldn’t read. So Sejong made up his mind: “Let’s create our own letters anyone can learn!” His brush began to trace little circles and lines, all on its own.

26
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:32,430
Every night, Sejong quietly studied. How does each sound leave the mouth? How can a shape hold it? Even when his eyes hurt and he was tired, he never gave up. Amazing, right?

27
00:06:32,130 --> 00:06:46,220
And finally! In the winter of 1443, Sejong completed twenty-eight new letters. Their name: “Hunminjeongeum” — “the right sounds to teach the people.”

28
00:06:46,220 --> 00:07:01,450
In Sejong’s mind lived a whole universe. He wanted to pack sky, earth, and people into just twenty-eight little letters. Now — shall we unlock the amazing secret, one by one?

29
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:13,520
To test the new letters, Sejong and his clever young scholars wrote a book with them. And wonderfully — any words at all flowed right onto the page!

30
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:23,320
But some officials shook their heads. “Chinese characters are enough — why make new letters?” they said.

31
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:37,200
Really, they just didn’t like easy new letters. Only those who knew hard Chinese characters could show off as clever. “Letters mustn’t be too easy!” they insisted.

32
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:46,390
Again and again they objected. As Sejong listened and listened, something slowly rose up inside him.

33
00:07:48,990 --> 00:08:03,800
Sejong said it clearly: “What’s wrong with easy letters? If everyone can read and write, those are the BEST letters!” His heart for the people would not waver one bit.

34
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:10,810
The room fell quiet. Before Sejong’s firm resolve, everyone could only nod.

35
00:08:10,810 --> 00:08:18,840
Sejong never wavered. He had only one thought: “These letters are for the people.”

36
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:37,660
Now, the secret! The consonants copy the shape of our mouth. ‘ㄱ’ is the tongue blocking the throat, ‘ㄴ’ the tongue touching the teeth, ‘ㅁ’ the shape of the lips! Cool, huh?

37
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:55,390
And when a sound grows stronger, just add a line! ‘ㄴ’ plus a line is ‘ㄷ’, add another and it’s ‘ㅌ’! Clever letters you can read just by their shape.

38
00:08:55,090 --> 00:09:10,580
The vowels are even cooler! A round ‘ㆍ’ like the sky, a flat ‘ㅡ’ like the earth, a standing ‘ㅣ’ like a person. The whole world, in just three little strokes!

39
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:24,550
Mix the three and you get ‘ㅏ, ㅓ, ㅗ, ㅜ’… every sound! Simple letters that can write anything — like magic.

40
00:09:24,250 --> 00:09:39,500
In 1446, Sejong made a book explaining the letters and gave it to the world. “The clever learn it in a day, anyone in ten!” The people were overjoyed.

41
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:57,790
With the new letters came wonderful things! People wrote songs and storybooks in Hangeul. Sejong wrote a beautiful song too: “A tree with deep roots never sways in the wind.”

42
00:09:57,790 --> 00:10:06,470
Sejong even added Hangeul to the exams for officials. And so, more and more people came to know it.

43
00:10:06,170 --> 00:10:15,480
Sejong grew old, and his eyes hurt a lot. But for his people, he never let his books go, right to the end.

44
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:27,970
In the spring of 1450, King Sejong peacefully closed his eyes. Though he left us — his love for the people lives on forever, inside the letters.

45
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:59,700
For 580 years, thanks to this wonderful king, even the children of the poorest, humblest homes could play in the alleys, writing letters in the dirt with wooden sticks. This was the great gift King Sejong gave to all his people and to every generation to come.

46
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:13,590
Years passed, and the whole world saw how amazing Hangeul is. UNESCO named it a “world treasure” and even created a prize in Sejong’s name.

47
00:11:13,290 --> 00:11:25,660
Letters born from the shape of our mouth, from sky and earth and people. Small and simple — yet inside them lives a warm heart for everyone.

48
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:44,510
Every October 9th is Hangeul Day! We share our hearts in Hangeul — Sejong’s gift, the world’s coolest letters, made from mouth shapes and sky, earth, and person. Thank you, King Sejong!

